  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Japanese Cowboy**: back after 465 archived shows (7046 days) [5]\n- **Now I'm Freaking Out**: back after 46 archived shows (2350 days) [5]\n- **Puerto Rican Power**: back after 40 archived shows (2135 days) [5]\n- **Don't Laugh, I love You**: back after 51 archived shows (2355 days); rare: 9 archived performances [5]\n- **Boy's Club**: back after 57 archived shows (2402 days) [5]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: How High Can You Fly? [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2016-02-12.dpa4018a.flac16** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 33 songs; 145 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says the DPA microphones capture the room very well, about as good as an audience recording gets [4]\n- **ween2016-02-12.akg391b.flac16**: source not stated; 33 songs; 145 min [2]\n- **Ween2016-02-12.flac16**: source not stated; 33 songs; 145 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Confetti cannons fired right in front of the microphones at the back of the soundboard during this song [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2016-02-12.dpa4018a.flac16**: taped by Scott Schneider; transferred by Scott Schneider; source: DPA 4018a(behind SBD DFC@11' 34cm/60deg)->Sonosax SX-M2->Mytek 192->HD-P2(24/96) [1]\n- **ween2016-02-12.akg391b.flac16**: taped by James E; transferred by BlingFree; source: AKG 391b (PAS) > Zoom H6 (24/96) [2]. Also: Recorded with an AKG 391b into a Zoom H6 at 24/96, placed in the front left soundboard cage; Lineage: r8brain PRO, then Wavelab 6, then CD Wave Editor to FLAC 6, tagged with Live Show Tagger [2]\n- **Ween2016-02-12.flac16**: taped by scottsch; transferred by theworstmanalive [3]",
